ed to"},{"name":"failed_to_copy_some_files","value":"Failed to Copy some files."},{"name":"failed_to_move_some_files","value":"Failed to Move some files."},{"name":"faq","value":"FAQ"},{"name":"faq_ans_1","value":"➤ The GPS Map Camera app is a mobile application that allows users to capture photos with geotags, including GPS location, date, time, and informative details. It enhances your photography experience by adding informative stamps to your images."},{"name":"faq_ans_10","value":"➤ No, you must visit the actual place and be within the range you set to use a Manual Location. This ensures that the address stamped on your photos reflects the real location where the photo was taken."},{"name":"faq_ans_11","value":"\"➤ Yes, you can add a Manual Location for another place while you’re at your current location. However, you will only be able to use that Manual Location when you are physically near that place and within the range you set. If you are not in the range of that location, you won't be able to use it to stamp photos.\""},{"name":"faq_ans_12","value":"➤ In the GPS map camera, there are four types of maps available such as (standard map, Satellite Map, Hybrid Map, Terrain Map) you can use any map type to make your image stylish and important."},{"name":"faq_ans_14","value":"➤ The difference between the \\\"Advance template\\\" and the \\\"Classic template\\\" lies primarily in their layout design."},{"name":"faq_ans_15","value":"➤ If you need an ad-free experience, then you need to purchase the pro version of the GPS map camera. The premium version allows you to use this app without ad interruption."},{"name":"faq_ans_16","value":"➤ To reduce your photo size, go to Settings, find the Image Quality option, and choose the desired quality level: High, Medium, or Low, as you need. Selecting Medium or Low will reduce the file size while maintaining good image quality."},{"name":"faq_ans_2","value":"➤ The Manual Location feature allows users to edit and customize the location details stamped on their photos. This feature is particularly useful for adding personalized addresses to photos taken for events, business purposes, or creative projects."},{"name":"faq_ans_4","value":"➤ “In Range” means you’ve added a Manual Location with a specific range (like 100m), and your current location is inside that range."},{"name":"faq_ans_5","value":"\"➤ “Out of Range” means you’ve added Manual Locations, but your current location is not inside the range of any of added manual location. Since your current location is outside the range of all Manual Locations, you cannot use them on your photos until you go inside one of those location's range.\""},{"name":"faq_ans_6","value":"\"➤ You cannot select an Out of Range Manual Location because your current location is outside the range you set for manual locations. Once you're inside the range, you’ll be able to select and use that Manual Location on your photos.\""},{"name":"faq_ans_7","value":"➤ The range ensures that you are physically inside the location range you set. This keeps your photos authentic by making sure the address stamped on the photo matches where you are. You need to be within the specified range (for example, 100m) to use the Manual Location."},{"name":"faq_ans_8","value":"➤ By requiring you to be physically within range of the location you set, the feature ensures that the address stamped on your photos is accurate and can’t be manipulated. This adds authenticity and trustworthiness to your work photos, as the location data is real."},{"name":"faq_ans_9","value":"➤ To maintain location accuracy, the short address (City, State, Country) cannot be changed. This ensures the photo’s location is real and prevents from stamping photos with false or incorrect city or country information."},{"name":"faq_cat_all","value":"All"},{"name":"faq_cat_general","value":"General"},{"name":"faq_cat_manual_location","value":"Manual Location"},{"name":"faq_cat_map_photos","value":"Map &amp; Photo